WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.280
A Paramecium is one cell.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.160
You are made of about 30 trillion.

3
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.800
You both do the same jobs, so why do you need so many cells?

4
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:16.373
Both of you share one list of life jobs.

5
00:00:17.573 --> 00:00:19.713
You move, get food and exchange gases.

6
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:23.133
You get rid of wastes and extra water.

7
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.533
You respond to the world, and you reproduce.

8
00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:31.257
Watch one Paramecium do every job on that list.

9
00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:35.357
Short, hair-like parts called cilia cover the whole cell.

10
00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:38.837
They beat together and push it through the water.

11
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.600
It sweeps bacteria into a groove on one side.

12
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.400
They end up in small sacs called food vacuoles, where the food is digested.

13
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.430
Oxygen passes in across its outer membrane.

14
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.150
Carbon dioxide passes out the same way.

15
00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.350
No lungs, no gills, just the surface of one cell.

16
00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:06.653
Pond water keeps moving into the cell.

17
00:01:07.913 --> 00:01:12.953
A sac called a contractile vacuole fills with the extra water and squeezes it out.

18
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:17.133
Bits of food it cannot digest leave through a small opening.

19
00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:22.917
When it bumps into something, it backs up, turns, and swims off another way.

20
00:01:24.177 --> 00:01:25.177
That is a response.

21
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.500
And it can divide.

22
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.260
It pinches in the middle and becomes two cells.

23
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.200
Every job is done inside one cell, with different parts helping.

24
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.650
So why not keep one cell and make it bigger?

25
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:44.110
Could one cell grow as big as you and still do every job?

26
00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:46.590
Pause and decide.

27
00:01:52.967 --> 00:01:55.607
Not by just growing bigger in every direction.

28
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:01.667
Food and oxygen must cross the cell’s surface, its outer membrane, to get in.

29
00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:06.047
Carbon dioxide and many wastes pass out across it.

30
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:09.417
Now let the cell grow, but keep its shape.

31
00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:14.997
Its inside grows faster than its surface, and its middle gets farther away.

32
00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:21.157
Without special features, a big enough cell may not get food and oxygen to its

33
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:22.157
middle fast enough.

34
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.480
So your big body is not one giant cell.

35
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.420
It is made of many small cells.

36
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.920
Each one sits close to the watery fluid that brings it food and oxygen.

37
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:37.063
Many cells bring a second gain.

38
00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:39.723
They can split up the job list.

39
00:02:41.023 --> 00:02:43.443
Different groups of cells can take on different jobs.

40
00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:47.587
Sharing the work this way is called division of labor.

41
00:02:48.907 --> 00:02:51.767
A Paramecium does the whole list in one small cell.

42
00:02:53.027 --> 00:02:56.447
You do the same list with trillions of small cells that share it.
